@page "/money-stays-safe"
@layout PublicLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Money Stays Safe - Email Money App</PageTitle>

<section class="brochure-information-page">
    <h2>We Don’t Touch the Money</h2>

    <div class="brochure-information-copy">
        <p>EMA is purposely designed to stay away from handling the money.</p>

        <p>
            We promote this use of eTransfers &amp; Pre-Authorized Debits, and we have very safe,
            effective &amp; financially attractive ways to support those giving methods.
        </p>

        <p>
            Having said that, we also recognize that EMA needs to support Credit and Debit cards, so
            we plan to add that to EMA-Giving in the coming months. Our implementation will be
            different from most other church management systems and fundraising platforms, as our
            implementation will allow EMA to avoid handing the details of credit and debit cards as
            well.
        </p>

        <p>
            Cheques have been a significant method of giving for some non-profits, and of course
            we can enter donations by cash and cheque into our system. We thought about
            automating cheques as well, as today’s technology would allow us to do that. However,
            the use of cheques is inconsistent with our commitment to promote the use of payment
            methods that don’t involve cash and cheques, so for now at least, automating cheques is
            not on our horizon.
        </p>

        <p>
            Cash and cheques introduce significant hidden costs, security risks, and administrative
            burden for non-profits. Processing physical currency and paper cheques requires
            manual handling, reconciliation time, and secure storage or physical bank visits—all of
            which increase overhead and elevate the risk of human error or loss. Cheques are
            vulnerable to delays, clearing fees, and fraud, while cash offers zero audit trail.
        </p>

        <p>
            Our parent company, EMA Nonprofit Technologies, uses a digital business banking
            platform that has no physical bank branches, does not support physical cash deposits,
            cash withdrawals, or in-person teller services. All operations, deposits, transfers, and
            expense management run entirely through digital rails (such as electronic funds
            transfers and pre-authorized debits (PADs).
        </p>
    </div>

    <p class="brochure-information-emphasis">
        EMA never holds, freezes, or delays donated funds.
    </p>
</section>
